<Page title="Changelog · OpenLeo" description="What's new in each version of OpenLeo." current="changelog">
<h1 class="text-[36px] leading-tight font-semibold tracking-[-0.03em]">Changelog</h1>
<p class="text-[13px] text-ink-3">What's new in each version. The app updates itself, or download the latest from <a href="https://github.com/ancs21/openleo/releases/latest">GitHub</a>.</p>
<h2>0.10.10</h2>
<p class="text-[13px] text-ink-3">9 October 2026</p>
<ul>
<li>The first release built from the public repository. The app itself is the same as 0.10.9.</li>
</ul>
<h2>0.10.9</h2>
<p class="text-[13px] text-ink-3">9 October 2026</p>
<ul>
<li>The first desktop release, for Mac (Apple silicon), Windows and Linux.</li>
<li>Setup walks you through giving your agents a computer, with Apple's container tool on new Macs or Docker everywhere else. It downloads the computer ready-made for your chip, and on Windows it can switch Docker to the Linux containers it needs.</li>
<li>OpenLeo updates itself. It looks for a new version when it opens and every few hours, gets it ready in the background, then offers a restart. You can also choose <b>Check for Updates…</b> in the OpenLeo menu or the menu bar icon.</li>
<li>The Mac app is signed and checked by Apple, so it opens without the "unidentified developer" warning.</li>
<li><b>Open on your other devices</b>: use OpenLeo from your phone or laptop, wherever you are, through Tailscale. Turn it on from your account menu and scan the code. See the <a href="./blog/tailscale">guide</a>.</li>
</ul>
